president biden is staying at camp david  this weekend he's meeting with his  national security team on the ukraine  crisis but there are major domestic  issues that have plunged the president's  approval rating to its lowest point  since he took office natalie brand is at  the white house to review mr biden's  first year in office and what's ahead  natalie good morning  good morning michelle president biden's  recent polling numbers have dipped under  the weight of the pandemic the economy a  spike in inflation challenges he  continues to face as he enters into a  key midterm elections year  just look at what we've accomplished  together so far now officially in his  second year in the white house president  biden touted one of his biggest wins to  date speaking friday before a conference  of the nation's mayors the  infrastructure law is a perfect example  of what we can achieve when we tackle  problems the way mayors do we came  together  democrats and republicans  and did something about it  but that bipartisanship was short-lived  and president biden's ambitious  legislative agenda has come to a  grinding halt facing pushback from even  some members of his own party they would  use the nuclear option to override a  rule that  we have used ourselves  but now seem to find unacceptable on  this vote on wednesday senate democrats  were two votes shy of changing  filibuster rules to allow voting rights  legislation to move forward  and with the president's massive social  spending and climate plan stalled he  acknowledged the bill likely won't pass  as is we're going to have to  probably  break it up the president says he will  ramp up efforts to take the case to the  american people he's ready to get out  there in the country and telling more of  the story of what we've accomplished but  also the work we have to date president  biden's tenure in office thus far has  been  pretty much as uneven as the stock  market george washington university  professor laura brown points to some  factors outside of the president's  control what really has i think  bedeviled president biden is a lack of  consistency and a lack of persistence on  the issues that americans care the most  about  which are namely the pandemic and the  economy  and president biden this week  acknowledged the continued frustration  among americans between covid fatigue  rising prices he said this week that  fixing the supply chain tops his short  list of priorities dana  all right natalie thank you
 

